<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Results registry — status</title>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<style>
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; --ink: #1a1a1a; --ink2: #666; --bg: #fafafa; --panel: #fff; --line: #e3e3e3; --head: #f0f0f0; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root { --ink: #ececec; --ink2: #a8a8a8; --bg: #131313; --panel: #1c1c1c; --line: #2e2e2e; --head: #222; } }
  body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 1200px; color: var(--ink); background: var(--bg); padding: 0 1rem; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; } h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin-top: 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 0.2rem; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 0.85rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: var(--head); }
  .stamp { color: var(--ink2); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .banner { padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; margin: 1rem 0; }
  .paused { background: #ffe9e6; border: 1px solid #e0776b; color: #1a1a1a; }
  .deprecated { background: #fff6dd; border: 1px solid #d9b74a; color: #1a1a1a; }
  .empty { color: var(--ink2); font-style: italic; }
  .note { color: var(--ink2); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .stale { background: #fff6dd; border-left: 3px solid #d9b74a; padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem; color: #1a1a1a; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { .stale { background: #2a2410; color: #ececec; } }
  .late { background: #ffe9e6; border-left: 3px solid #e0776b; padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem; color: #1a1a1a; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { .late { background: #2e1512; color: #ececec; } }
  code { background: var(--head); padding: 0 0.2rem; border-radius: 3px; }
  .tiles { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(11rem, 1fr)); gap: 0.6rem; margin: 1rem 0; }
  .tile { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem; }
  .tile b { display: block; font-size: 1.3rem; } .tile span { color: var(--ink2); font-size: 0.8rem; }
  tr.red td:first-child { border-left: 3px solid #e0776b; } tr.amber td:first-child { border-left: 3px solid #d9b74a; }
  tr.standing td:first-child { border-left: 3px solid #7a9cc6; } tr.green td:first-child { border-left: 3px solid transparent; }
  .level-red { color: #c0392b; font-weight: 600; } .level-amber { color: #a87b00; font-weight: 600; } .level-green { color: var(--ink2); }
  .level-standing { color: #3b6ea5; font-weight: 600; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Results registry — status</h1>
<p class="stamp">Built {{ built_utc }} · schema v{{ schema_version }} · index head <code>{{ index_head_seq }}</code> · paper-input head <code>{{ head_seq }}</code> ·
   root <code>{{ root }}</code>{% if open_round %} · open round <code>{{ open_round.round_id }}</code>{% endif %}</p>

{% if paused %}
<div class="banner paused"><strong>Ingest paused</strong> since {{ paused.paused_utc }} — {{ paused.reason }}
 (free {{ (paused.free_bytes / 1073741824) | round(2) }} GB). Records stay in the spool; nothing is lost.</div>
{% endif %}
{% if schema_drift or schema_version != schema_version_code %}
<div class="banner paused"><strong>Schema drift</strong> — writers refuse this database until <code>registry migrate</code> brings it to the code's shape
{% if schema_version != schema_version_code %}(schema v{{ schema_version }}, code v{{ schema_version_code }}: a migration is pending){% endif %}{% if schema_drift %}
(<code>registry migrate --plan --sql</code> renders the missing migration; landed migration files are frozen):
<ul>{% for line in schema_drift %}<li>{{ line }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% else %}.{% endif %}
Nothing is written meanwhile; records stay in the log.</div>
{% endif %}
{% if slurm_only.maintenance.set %}
<div class="banner {% if slurm_only.maintenance.stale %}paused{% else %}deprecated{% endif %}"><strong>Maintenance flag set</strong> since {{ slurm_only.maintenance.since_utc }}{% if slurm_only.maintenance.age_s is not none %} ({{ slurm_only.maintenance.age_s }} s ago){% else %} (age unknown: the stamp does not parse){% endif %}{% if slurm_only.maintenance.reason %} — {{ slurm_only.maintenance.reason }}{% endif %}{% if slurm_only.maintenance.window %}; window <code>{{ slurm_only.maintenance.window }}</code>{% endif %}{% if slurm_only.maintenance.adapters %}; adapters <code>{{ slurm_only.maintenance.adapters }}</code>{% endif %}.
 The harvester exits at the door while <code>state/maintenance.json</code> exists (nothing is pulled or folded); a landing window writes it before stopping the timers and its trap removes it.{% if slurm_only.maintenance.stale %} <strong>STALE</strong>: older than {{ slurm_only.maintenance.stale_after_s }} s — a window left it behind (its trap never ran); check <code>windows/chain.log</code> and remove the flag only when no window is running.{% endif %}</div>
{% endif %}
{% if slurm_only.config.removed_table %}
<div class="banner paused"><strong>Configuration refused</strong> — <code>{{ slurm_only.config.path }}</code> still carries the removed <code>{{ slurm_only.config.table }}</code> table ({{ slurm_only.config.table_keys | join(', ') or 'no keys' }}): every registry command that reads the configuration refuses by name (<code>registry &lt;cmd&gt;: configuration REFUSED</code>), and this page renders on the budget defaults. Convert it: <code>python3 {{ slurm_only.config.converter }} --root {{ root }}</code>, then <code>registry config --check</code> (the cutover window's <code>-- config convert</code> stage does both).</div>
{% elif slurm_only.config.error %}
<div class="banner paused"><strong>Configuration unreadable</strong> — <code>{{ slurm_only.config.path }}</code> does not parse ({{ slurm_only.config.error }}): every registry command that reads it refuses; this page renders on the budget defaults.</div>
{% endif %}
<div class="banner deprecated">{{ deprecation_notice }}</div>

<div class="tiles">
  <div class="tile"><b>{{ in_flight | length }}</b><span>runs in flight</span></div>
  <div class="tile"><b>{{ roster_gaps | length }}</b><span>roster gaps (open round)</span></div>
  <div class="tile"><b>{{ pending_count }}</b><span>pending judgments (instrument judge)</span></div>
  <div class="tile"><b>{{ refused | length }}</b><span>refused records</span></div>
  <div class="tile"><b>{{ blocked | length }}</b><span>blocked records</span></div>
  <div class="tile"><b>{{ not_measured_total }}</b><span>degeneration pairs not measured</span></div>
  <div class="tile"><b>{{ decode_unmatched_total }}</b><span>runs whose sent decode matches no policy row (ambiguous + no_match)</span></div>
  <div class="tile"><b>{{ bon_decode_precedence_violations | length }}</b><span>best-of-N keys reading T = 1 beside a selected vendor preset (the rule says none)</span></div>
  <div class="tile"><b>{{ source_coverage.without_adapter | length if not source_coverage.error else '?' }}</b><span>declared sources without an adapter</span></div>
  <div class="tile"><b>{{ rulings_relayed_unconfirmed | length }}</b><span>relayed rulings awaiting the user's confirmation</span></div>
  <div class="tile"><b>{{ disk.free_gb }} GB</b><span>free disk (floor {{ disk.floor_gb }} GB; headroom {{ disk.headroom_gb }} GB)</span></div>
  <div class="tile"><b>{{ snapshot_current or '—' }}</b><span>CURRENT snapshot</span></div>
  <div class="tile"><b class="level-{{ slurm_only.level }}">{{ slurm_only.n_problems }}</b><span>cluster-side problems (store authority, replica check, reads reservation and receipts, maintenance flag, configuration)</span></div>
</div>
{% if sections_from_cache %}
<p class="note stale">Rendered within budget ({{ budgets.render_budget_s | int }} s; {{ budgets.section_budget_s | int }} s per section): <strong>{{ sections_from_cache | length }}</strong> section(s) show their last good rows this render —
{% for n in sections_from_cache %}<code>{{ n }}</code>{% if section_state[n].as_of %} (as of {{ section_state[n].as_of }}){% else %} (no cached rows yet){% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
Cached-with-refresh set: {% if heavy_set %}{% for n in heavy_set %}<code>{{ n }}</code>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% else %}empty{% endif %};
last exact refresh {{ heavy_state.refreshed_utc or 'never' }}{% if heavy_state.head is not none %} at ledger head <code>{{ heavy_state.head }}</code>{% endif %} (<code>registry status --refresh-heavy</code>, every 6 h while the head moves).</p>
{% endif %}

{% macro mark(name) -%}
{% set st = section_state[name] %}
{% if st.state == 'cached' %}<p class="note stale">Last good rows as of <strong>{{ st.as_of }}</strong>; {{ st.reason }}.{% if st.in_heavy_set %} In the cached-with-refresh set: recomputed exactly by <code>registry status --refresh-heavy</code>.{% endif %}</p>
{% elif st.state == 'no_cache' %}<p class="note stale"><strong>Not computed this render and no cached rows yet</strong> ({{ st.reason }}): the table below is empty because nothing has been computed for it within budget, not because there is nothing to show; <code>registry status --refresh-heavy</code> fills it.</p>
{% elif st.state == 'error' %}<p class="note stale"><strong>Query failed this render</strong> ({{ st.reason }}): the row below is the error, not the section's rows; its last good rows, if any, stay cached and are shown by a render this query is skipped in.</p>
{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro table(rows, cols=None) -%}
{% if rows %}
<table>
<tr>{% for k in (cols or rows[0].keys()) %}<th>{{ k }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% for r in rows %}<tr>{% for k in (cols or rows[0].keys()) %}<td>{{ r[k] if r[k] is not none else '' }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% else %}<p class="empty">none</p>{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

<h2>Runs in flight</h2>
{{ mark('in_flight') }}
{{ table(in_flight, ['run_id', 'lifecycle_state', 'substrate', 'cluster_job_id', 'node_hostname', 'last_event_state', 'last_scheduler_state', 'age_s']) }}

<h2>Roster gaps (open round: entries with neither a judged run nor a disposition)</h2>
{{ mark('roster_gaps') }}
{{ table(roster_gaps, ['roster_entry_id', 'comparison_id', 'model_id', 'object_id', 'eval_id', 'instrument_id', 'source_citation']) }}

<h2>Objects in / out of the current round (derived: the runs the flag selects and the rulings naming the object; never hand-set)</h2>
{{ mark('paper_objects') }}
{% if paper_objects_available %}
{{ table(paper_objects, ['object_id', 'paper_label', 'object_kind', 'in_paper', 'n_runs', 'n_runs_in_paper', 'comparison_ids_json', 'excluding_ruling_ids_json', 'run_excluding_ruling_ids_json']) }}
{% else %}
<p class="empty">roster not loaded — the round's object roster (<code>{{ paper_objects_name }}</code>) is not in this database yet; this section is incomplete until it is.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Rulings of the open round (who they came from)</h2>
{{ mark('rulings') }}
<p class="note"><code>provenance</code>: <code>relayed</code> = a peer session relayed the user's words and the user has not yet confirmed the
registry's reading of them (listed first; <code>relayed_by</code> and <code>message_utc</code> name the message); <code>peer_encoded</code> = a peer
session's committed paper code declares the user's ruling (<code>ruled_by</code> names the session and the commit); <code>user_direct</code> = the user
ruled it in this session; <code>in_ruled_by_prose</code> = a ruling transcribed before 2026-09-17 whose provenance is in its <code>ruled_by</code> text.
<code>n_runs_decided</code> counts the runs whose paper membership this ruling decides today. <code>evidence_state</code> is the expiry evidence of a
self-retiring ruling, not its provenance.</p>
{% if rulings_relayed_unconfirmed %}<p class="note"><strong>{{ rulings_relayed_unconfirmed | length }} relayed ruling(s) await the user's confirmation.</strong></p>{% endif %}
{{ table(rulings, ['ruling_id', 'action', 'scope_kind', 'provenance', 'relayed_by', 'message_utc', 'confirmed_by_user', 'ruled_utc', 'ruled_by', 'evidence_state', 'expired_utc', 'n_runs_decided']) }}

<h2>Dispositions (sources that have not run: pending, held, not served, not applicable, declined)</h2>
{{ mark('dispositions') }}
{{ table(dispositions) }}

<h2>Paper parity gate runs</h2>
{{ mark('parity_gates') }}
{{ table(parity_gates) }}

<h2>Analyses (filed over ingested runs and objects)</h2>
{{ mark('analyses') }}
<p class="note">An analysis is a prefill-only or offline computation with results but no run of its own (D357): one <code>analysis</code> row per filing (<code>registry analysis file --spec</code>; records under <code>records/analyses/&lt;day&gt;/</code>, folded as ledger facts), its inputs in <code>analysis_input</code>, its registered files in <code>analysis_artifact</code>. <code>provenance</code> reads <code>relayed</code> when a peer session relayed the user's work (D83). <code>registry analysis list</code> reads the whole table.</p>
{% if analyses %}
<table>
<tr><th>name</th><th>code_sha</th><th>substrate</th><th>filed_utc</th><th>filed_by</th><th>provenance</th><th>n_runs</th><th>n_objects</th><th>n_artifacts</th><th>report</th><th>pages</th></tr>
{% for a in analyses %}{% if 'error' in a %}<tr><td colspan="11">{{ a.error }}</td></tr>{% else %}<tr><td>{{ a.name }}</td><td>{{ (a.code_sha or '')[:12] }}</td><td>{{ a.substrate }}</td><td>{{ a.filed_utc }}</td><td>{{ a.filed_by }}</td><td>{{ a.provenance }}{% if a.relayed_by %} (by {{ a.relayed_by }}){% endif %}</td><td>{{ a.n_runs }}</td><td>{{ a.n_objects }}</td><td>{{ a.n_artifacts }}</td><td>{% if a.report_uri %}<code>{{ a.report_uri }}</code>{% endif %}</td><td>{% for u in (a.page_urls or '').split(' ') if u %}<a href="{{ u }}">{{ u }}</a> {% endfor %}</td></tr>{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% else %}<p class="empty">none</p>{% endif %}

<h2>Refused records</h2>
{{ mark('refused') }}
{{ table(refused) }}

<h2>Blocked records (well-formed, parent not yet ingested)</h2>
{{ mark('blocked') }}
{{ table(blocked) }}

<h2>Refusals (facts): the judgments derived in the last {{ refusal_facts_window_s }} s</h2>
{{ mark('refusal_facts') }}
<p class="note">Every refusal judgment is a record in the log (<code>records/harvester/&lt;day&gt;/record_refusal-*.jsonl</code>) and a row of <code>record_refusal_fact</code>, keyed by the refused record and the judging stamp, so every mirror and every rebuild carry it; the table above keeps the CURRENT judgment per record. <code>still_refused</code> = this judgment is the record's current one; <code>backfilled</code> = a refusal recorded before the stamp was kept, materialized under <code>unverified</code>. Shown: the facts whose cycle is within {{ refusal_facts_window_s }} s (3 × the harvest cadence) — {{ refusal_facts_recent | length }} of the {{ refusal_facts | length }} most recent; the whole ledger is <code>registry refusals list|explain|summary</code>.</p>
{{ table(refusal_facts_recent, ['record_uri', 'record_type', 'field', 'reason', 'judged_with', 'refused_utc', 'cycle_utc', 'still_refused', 'backfilled']) }}

<h2>Recent ingests</h2>
{{ mark('recent_ingests') }}
{{ table(recent_ingests) }}

<h2>Superseded readings</h2>
{{ mark('superseded') }}
{{ table(superseded, ['kind', 'id', 'superseded_by', 'ruling_id', 'ruling_action', 'ruling_reason', 'state']) }}

<h2>Snapshot freshness per destination</h2>
{{ mark('snapshots') }}
<p class="note">CURRENT: <code>{{ snapshot_current or 'none' }}</code>. A full set carries every table of record's Parquet (not the history ledger, which no snapshot ships); a run-level set only the run-scale tables and the run-level SQLite.</p>
{{ table(snapshot_pushes, ['destination', 'snapshot_id', 'pushed_utc', 'ok', 'reclaimed', 'leases_blocking', 'error']) }}
<p class="note">Resident on the grading host:</p>
{{ table(snapshots_resident, ['snapshot_id', 'scope', 'ingest_seq', 'built_utc', 'age_s', 'files', 'leases']) }}
<p class="note">Recorded snapshots:</p>
{{ table(snapshots, ['snapshot_id', 'scope', 'head_ingest_seq', 'built_utc']) }}

<h2>Live snapshot leases</h2>
<p class="note">A lease keeps its snapshot directory resident. The heartbeat age is diagnostic; a Modal lease is released only by its reader or a verified terminal call.</p>
{{ table(leases) }}

<h2>Mirror lag (record log fan-out)</h2>
<p class="note">Latest manifest: <code>{{ latest_manifest or 'none' }}</code>. Lag = files the latest manifest names that the destination lacks or corrupts; unsynced local files ride the next sync.</p>
{{ table(mirror_lag) }}

<h2>Mirror acknowledgements (verified syncs)</h2>
{{ mark('mirror_acks') }}
{{ table(mirror_acks) }}

<h2>Disk headroom</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>free</th><th>guard floor</th><th>headroom above the floor</th><th>database</th><th>a full snapshot needs</th><th>resident budget</th></tr>
<tr><td>{{ disk.free_gb }} GB</td><td>{{ disk.floor_gb }} GB</td><td>{{ disk.headroom_gb }} GB</td><td>{{ disk.db_gb }} GB</td><td>{{ disk.snapshot_need_gb }} GB</td><td>{{ disk.budget_gb }} GB</td></tr>
</table>
{% if footprint %}
<p class="note">Last snapshot cycle ({{ footprint.utc }}, {{ footprint.snapshot_id }}, scope {{ footprint.scope }}): peak {{ (footprint.peak_bytes / 1073741824) | round(3) }} GB of the {{ (footprint.budget_bytes / 1073741824) | round(0) }} GB budget{% if footprint.error %} — <strong>{{ footprint.error }}</strong>{% endif %}.</p>
{% else %}<p class="empty">no snapshot cycle recorded yet</p>{% endif %}

<h2>Paper rebuild</h2>
{% if paper_rebuild.result %}
<p><code>{{ paper_rebuild.result }}</code></p>
{% else %}<p class="empty">no rebuild recorded yet</p>{% endif %}
<p class="note">last built head: <code>{{ paper_rebuild.last_head or '—' }}</code> · failed head: <code>{{ paper_rebuild.failed_head or '—' }}</code> · head file: <code>{{ paper_rebuild.head_file or '—' }}</code></p>

<h2>Timer health (last run per command)</h2>
<p class="{% if harvest_cycle.state == 'late' %}late{% elif harvest_cycle.state == 'unknown' %}stale{% else %}note{% endif %}" id="harvester-cycle">
<strong>Harvester</strong> — last completed cycle:
{% if harvest_cycle.last_completed_cycle_utc %}<code>{{ harvest_cycle.last_completed_cycle_utc }}</code>, {{ harvest_cycle.age_s }} s ago{% if harvest_cycle.elapsed_s is not none %} (took {{ harvest_cycle.elapsed_s }} s{% if harvest_cycle.files is not none %}, {{ harvest_cycle.files }} file(s){% endif %}{% if harvest_cycle.revisions_applied is not none %}, {{ harvest_cycle.revisions_applied }} revision director{{ 'y' if harvest_cycle.revisions_applied == 1 else 'ies' }} / bundle(s){% endif %}{% if harvest_cycle.refused is not none %}, refused {{ harvest_cycle.refused }} this cycle{% if harvest_cycle.refusal_facts is not none %} and wrote {{ harvest_cycle.refusal_facts }} refusal fact(s){% endif %}{% endif %}){% endif %}{% else %}<strong>none recorded yet</strong> (a cycle records itself only when it runs to completion){% endif %}.
{% if harvest_cycle.state == 'late' %}<strong>LATE</strong>: older than {{ harvest_cycle.late_after_s }} s, {{ 3 }} × the expected {{ harvest_cycle.cadence_s }} s between completed cycles — a cycle its unit kills at <code>TimeoutStartSec</code> completes nothing and moves no stamp; check <code>journalctl --user -u registry-harvest.service</code> and <code>state/metrics.jsonl</code> (<code>kind = "bundle"</code> lines name each revision directory folded).{% endif %}
WAL: <code>{{ wal_bytes }}</code> bytes ({{ wal_gb }} GB) in <code>registry.sqlite-wal</code> -- checkpointed at the end of every completed harvester cycle and after a landing window's drain; a file that only grows means readers hold it (checkpoint starvation).
{% if harvest_cycle.stopped %}The last cycle stopped on its <code>{{ harvest_cycle.stopped }}</code>{% if harvest_cycle.budget_s %} ({{ harvest_cycle.budget_s }} s){% endif %} and left {{ harvest_cycle.revisions_deferred_budget or 0 }} revision director{{ 'y' if harvest_cycle.revisions_deferred_budget == 1 else 'ies' }} / bundle(s) and {{ harvest_cycle.plain_files_deferred_budget or 0 }} plain file(s) for the next; everything it folded is committed.{% endif %}
</p>
{{ table(timers) }}

<h2>Cluster reads (the latest landing window's Slurm-sharded reads of the heavy adapters)</h2>
{% if cluster_reads.present %}
<p class="note">Window <code>{{ cluster_reads.window }}</code> built {{ cluster_reads.built_utc }} on tree <code>{{ (cluster_reads.tree_sha or '')[:9] }}</code>{% if cluster_reads.job_id %}, array job <code>{{ cluster_reads.job_id }}</code>{% endif %}. Route <strong>cluster</strong> = read on cluster A against pinned, verified store generations (K shards); <strong>grading_host</strong> = NOT read this window: the grading host reads no store (registry-slurm-only S2), the reason beside it. A refusal names why an adapter was recorded refused instead of read (a declaration, a refused component, a stale copy, a failed shard or pull); the window ends ABORTED with the refused adapters named.</p>
{{ table(cluster_reads.rows, ['adapter', 'route', 'shards', 'reason', 'refusals', 'pins']) }}
{% if cluster_reads.stages %}<p class="note">Stages: {% for name, st in cluster_reads.stages.items() %}<code>{{ name }}</code> {{ st.utc }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>{% endif %}
{% else %}<p class="empty">no cluster-read window recorded yet{% if cluster_reads.error %} ({{ cluster_reads.error }}){% endif %}</p>{% endif %}

{% macro ltable(rows, cols) -%}
{% if rows %}
<table>
<tr>{% for k in cols %}<th>{{ k }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% for r in rows %}<tr class="{{ r.level or 'green' }}">{% for k in cols %}<td>{% if k == 'level' %}<span class="level-{{ r.level or 'green' }}">{{ r.level or 'green' }}</span>{% elif r[k] is sameas true %}yes{% elif r[k] is sameas false %}no{% else %}{{ r[k] if r[k] is not none else '' }}{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% else %}<p class="empty">none</p>{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

<h2>Cluster reads, store authority and the replica (state files only; registry-slurm-only)</h2>
<p class="note">Overall <span class="level-{{ slurm_only.level }}">{{ slurm_only.level }}</span>: {{ slurm_only.n_problems }} problem(s){% if slurm_only.problems %} — {% for pr in slurm_only.problems %}{{ pr }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}.
Nothing here reads the database: <code>state/store_authority.json</code> (the last <code>registry stores check-authority</code>), <code>state/store_mirror.json</code> (the grading host mirror's last outcome per component), <code>state/replica_check.json</code> (the last Slurm live-DB step), <code>state/maintenance.json</code>, <code>config.toml</code>, and the reads namespace <code>{{ slurm_only.reads_dir }}</code> (the reservation and the read receipts). Gathered in {{ slurm_only.elapsed_ms }} ms.</p>

<h3>Store authority (per component: where the canonical copy is, and what stands beside its <code>current</code>)</h3>
{% set au = slurm_only.authority %}
{% if au.error %}<p class="note late"><strong>State file problem</strong>: {{ au.error }}.</p>{% endif %}
{% if au.present %}
<p class="note">Checked {{ au.checked_utc }}{% if au.checked_age_s is not none %} ({{ au.checked_age_s }} s ago){% endif %} on <code>{{ au.destination }}</code>: {{ au.n_components }} component(s), <strong class="level-{{ 'red' if au.n_problems else 'green' }}">{{ au.n_problems }} with a problem</strong>{% if au.problems %} — {% for pr in au.problems %}<code>{{ pr }}</code>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}.
A <code>cluster_a</code> component's canonical copy is the published generation on the cluster (<code>stores push</code> writes it; the grading host holds a verified mirror); <code>grading_host_copy</code> is carried there by the mirror; <code>cluster_a_origin</code> compares an in-place original. Red: <code>current</code> dangling, unverified, unsealed, without its PUBLISHED record, absent for a <code>cluster_a</code> component, or no grading host mirror; amber: a transitional carry past its deadline, or the grading host producer has unpushed changes. <code>mirror_outcome</code> is the last <code>stores</code> run's outcome for the component as <code>state/store_mirror.json</code> records it, whichever command stamped it — a <code>mirror</code> / <code>push</code> outcome, <code>check:&lt;state&gt;</code> (<code>stores check</code>) or <code>verify-authority:&lt;state&gt;</code> (the one-time move): <code>check:match</code> and <code>verify-authority:verified</code> are green, a run's in-flight <code>verify_submitted</code> / <code>verify_inline</code> amber, every failure red by name. <code>change_utc</code> is the producer's committed change the published generation carries (the S7 clock's start), <code>published_utc</code> when it was published.</p>
