<h3>Replica check (the last Slurm live-DB step of a landing)</h3>
{% set rp = slurm_only.replica %}
{% if rp.error %}<p class="note late"><strong>State file problem</strong>: {{ rp.error }}.</p>
{% elif rp.present %}
<p class="{% if rp.ok %}note{% else %}late{% endif %}"><strong>{% if rp.accepted_as == 'c1_class' %}equal modulo the C1 same-stamp class ({{ rp.n_movers }} movers, declared){% elif rp.equal %}equal{% else %}UNEQUAL{% endif %}{% if not rp.ok %} — refused ({{ rp.headline }}){% endif %}</strong> at {{ rp.utc }}{% if rp.age_s is not none %} ({{ rp.age_s }} s ago){% endif %}: branch <code>{{ rp.branch }}</code>, tip <code>{{ (rp.tip or '')[:12] }}</code>, job <code>{{ rp.job }}</code> {{ rp.job_state }}; projection <code>{{ rp.projection_version }}</code>, replica <code>{{ rp.replica_sha12 }}</code> vs head <code>{{ rp.head_sha12 }}</code> (head taken {{ rp.head_taken_utc }}, {{ rp.head_n_files }} files); generation <code>{{ rp.generation }}</code> (CURRENT <code>{{ rp.current_generation }}</code>, parent <code>{{ rp.parent_generation }}</code>), schema v{{ rp.schema_version }}; pytest rc {{ rp.pytest.rc }}, counts {{ rp.pytest.counts }}, expected skipped {{ rp.pytest.expected_skipped }}.
{% if rp.problems %}<br>{% for pr in rp.problems %}REFUSED: {{ pr }}{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
{% if rp.accepted_as == 'c1_class' %}<br>Accepted under the declared cutover allowance (D136): {{ rp.declaration }}.{% elif not rp.equal %}<br>An unequal check is a STOP (D12): no landing, nothing published; file the rows with the table and key, never seed the replica from a database copy.{% endif %}</p>
{% else %}<p class="empty">no Slurm live-DB step recorded on this root yet (<code>live_db_slurm.sh</code> writes <code>state/replica_check.json</code> at the end of every landing's step 3)</p>{% endif %}

<h3>Reads reservation (who owns the cluster-read namespace)</h3>
{% set rs = slurm_only.reservation %}
{% if rs.error %}<p class="note late"><strong>{{ rs.error }}</strong> — <code>{{ rs.reads_dir }}</code>.</p>
{% elif rs.held %}
<p class="{% if rs.state == 'live' %}note{% else %}stale{% endif %}">Held by <strong>{{ rs.owner }}</strong> <code>{{ rs.op_id }}</code> on <code>{{ rs.host }}</code> (pid {{ rs.pid }}) since {{ rs.started_utc }}{% if rs.age_s is not none %} ({{ rs.age_s }} s ago){% endif %}{% if rs.tree_sha %}, tree <code>{{ (rs.tree_sha or '')[:12] }}</code>{% endif %} — holder <strong>{{ rs.state }}</strong>{% if rs.state == 'stale' %} (its process is gone: the next tick or window cancels and confirms its jobs, then replaces it){% elif rs.state == 'unknown' %} (another host: not replaced from here){% endif %}.</p>
{% else %}<p class="empty">none held (<code>{{ rs.reads_dir }}</code>): no tick or window is reading the cluster now</p>{% endif %}

