<p class="note">A receipt row is red when it refused an adapter or stopped at a pull barrier, <span class="level-standing">standing</span> when it carries STANDING refusals and no new one, and keeps that color while it is listed (history); the section's level follows the NEWEST receipt, each adapter's newest result below and the receipt files that would not read, so an older red row is not a current problem and gets no headline.</p>
<p class="note">A <strong>standing</strong> refusal (the receipt's <code>standing_refusals</code> list, state <code>standing_refusal</code>) is one the cluster read re-confirmed byte for byte against the group's previous recorded refusal under the same inputs and tree: recorded here with the refusal and the recorded refusal it stands on (<code>prior_refusal</code>: its window and time; <code>standing_on</code>), never an abort of the window and never red — red means something NEW did not read. The cluster read writes such an adapter <code>read_whole: true</code> (so the tick leaves it alone); the list, not that bit, decides its state here: standing outranks whole. <code>refused_standing</code> is a different thing: the revision ids a pull left standing unread (<code>standing_unread</code>). The refusals that stand by design live with their reasons in the parked-by-name and pending-revisions sections below.</p>
<p class="note">Per adapter, the newest receipt that read it WHOLE (every shard ok, no refusal) — what the periodic tick's changed set and the fold-latency measurement rest on; <code>change_utc</code> / <code>published_utc</code> are the newest among that read's pins — beside the adapter's NEWEST result (<code>newest_state</code>: whole, refused, standing_refusal, standing_unread, partial, not_attempted). Red: the adapter's newest receipt refused it (a refusal in an older receipt that no later receipt replaced is still its newest result); amber: never read whole, or its newest read did not read it whole (a shard missing, ids left standing unread — an older whole read is the baseline, not the newest result); standing: its newest result is a re-confirmed refusal.</p>
{{ ltable(rc.adapters, ['adapter', 'utc', 'op_id', 'shards', 'revisions_pulled', 'pins', 'change_utc', 'published_utc', 'newest_op_id', 'newest_state', 'newest_refused', 'standing_on', 'standing_unread', 'level']) }}

