<h2>Best-of-N decode precedence (the vendor preset over T = 1 within one key)</h2>
{{ mark('bon_decode_precedence') }}
<p class="note">Ruling <code>{{ bon_decode_precedence_ruling_id }}</code> (the user, first-hand, 2026-09-28; D581): within one best-of-N key &mdash;
model, object and standup on <code>strongreject_bon</code> at the cap-4,096 climb and the N = 75 headline &mdash; the vendor-preset decode row is
the row a figure reads when one exists; the T = 1 climb row (<code>grandfathered_T1</code>) is the fallback only where no vendor-preset row
exists. A row is vendor-preset when its derived <code>decode_policy_id</code> names a <code>vendor_preset</code> policy or, where nothing matched,
when its <code>decode_source</code> is <code>generation_config</code>, <code>model_card</code> or <code>vendor_recommendation</code>
(<code>decode_precedence.decode_kind</code>). An unsteered anchor follows the steered row it pairs with and is never listed.
<strong>both_selected</strong>: a selected T = 1 row beside a selected vendor-preset row &mdash; the rule is broken; the remedy is a key-scoped
supersede of that key&rsquo;s T = 1 rows (<code>decode_precedence.supersede_ruling</code>, dry run first), never a blanket rule.
<strong>vendor_not_in_roster</strong>: a vendor-preset row exists for the key but the roster has not named it, so the T = 1 row is still the row
read &mdash; nothing to supersede yet. Violations: <strong>{{ bon_decode_precedence_violations | length }}</strong>; pending: {{ bon_decode_precedence_pending | length }}.
Empty is the invariant (<code>tests/test_registry_bon_decode_precedence.py</code> asserts it against the live database).</p>
